      "89": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "FEEDBACK LOOP\n\nIn this first example we use Perlin Noise to randomly move a circle across the screen.\nA Sine is used in conjunction with a Cross Fader node to fade between 2 different colors.\nThe output of the Video Mixer is patched back into the Video Mixer.\n\nAssignment: switch between feedback on the top and bottom layer, can you see the difference?"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 753.1090087890625,
          "width": 1930.4539794921875,
          "x": 630.2977294921875,
          "y": 630.7833251953125
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffff6a00",
        "constants": {},
